<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.13.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01089</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.13.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>7cd8f6e8-5a2d-4d70-a945-f8ed1661aac6</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>The graph of function \(H\) shows the height, in meters, of a rocket \(t\) seconds after it was launched.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <para><figure><media alt="Function on coordinate plane."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/45ceb267aeab7fc55ec544c03ba693d00323444a"/></media></figure></para>
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item>Find \(H(0)\) in meters.
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>15 meters</para>
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item>Which of the following describes the domain of this function?    </item>
  </list>
        <list>
        <item>\(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 35\)</item>
        <item>\(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 4.5\)</item>
        <item>\(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 2\)</item>
        <item>\(15 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 35\) </item>
      </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 4.5\); The domain includes all values from 0 to approximately 4.5, \(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 4.5\).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item>Which of the following describes the range of this function?    </item>
  </list>
</list>
      <list>
        <item>\(0 &amp;leq; y &amp;leq; 35\)</item>
        <item>\(0 &amp;leq; y &amp;leq; 4.5\)</item>
        <item>\(0 &amp;leq; y &amp;leq; 2\)</item>
        <item>\(15 &amp;leq; y &amp;leq; 35\)
          
        </item>
      </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(0 &amp;leq; y &amp;leq; 35\); The range includes all values from 0 to 35 meters, \(0 &amp;leq; y &amp;leq; 35\).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which of the following describes the domain of the function graphed below?
    
    <figure><media alt="Coordinate grid with wiggly graph. Horizontal axis by twos. Vertical axis by ones. Graphs starts around 2 comma 2 point 2 and ends around 7 comma 4."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4e8936b6cc6c10289d3e2b1c42310598da4d0999"/></media></figure></item>
</list>
    <list>
      <item>\(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 9\)</item>
      <item>\(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 4\)</item>
      <item>\(2 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 7\)</item>
      <item>\(2 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 4\)</item>
    </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(2 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 7\); The domain is all values from at least 2 to a maximum of 7, \( &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 7\). </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which of the following describes the range of the graph below?
    
    <figure><media alt="Coordinate grid with wiggly graph. Horizontal axis by twos. Vertical axis by ones. Graphs starts around 2 comma 2 point 2 and ends around 7 comma 4."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4e8936b6cc6c10289d3e2b1c42310598da4d0999"/></media></figure></item>
</list>
    <list>
      <item>\(2\leq y\leq4\)</item>
      <item>\(2\leq x\leq4\)</item>
      <item>\(2\leq y\leq7\)</item>
      <item>\(2\leq x\leq7\)</item>
    </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(2\leq y\leq4\). The range is all values from at least 2 to a maximum of 4, \(2\leq y\leq4\). </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item><emphasis>Select four</emphasis> of the values of the range for the function \(h\), graphed below.
    
    <figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/56d0af3118e4ed206a7350ae234fec3ae6c71cb5"/></media></figure></item>
</list>
    <list>
      <item>–5</item>
      <item>–3</item>
      <item>–2</item>
      <item>0</item>
      <item>2</item>
      <item>4</item>
      <item>5</item>
    </list>

<para><emphasis>Answers: </emphasis>–3, –2, 2, 4 </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which of the following is the domain of the function graphed below?
    
    <figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/0223a9341fcd7ca2dc3e2ddd4b42c389dbad097e"/></media></figure></item>
</list>
    <list>
      <item>\(-5\leq x\leq5\)</item>
      <item>\(-5 \leq x \leq 7\)</item>
      <item>\(-5 \leq y \leq 5\)</item>
      <item>\(-5 \leq y \leq 7\)</item>
    </list>
 
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(-5\leq x\leq5\) </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which of the following represents the domain of the function graphed below?
    
    <figure><media alt="GRAPH OF A LINE FOR ALL X GREATER THAN OR EQUAL TO 2, WITH POINT SHOWN AT (2 5), AND PASSING THROUGH THE POINTS (3, 8) AND (5, 14)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a79cc63c6acdd168fd53633b75e6c1594d031438"/></media></figure></item>
  </list>
  <list>
      <item>\(y\geq 5\)</item>
      <item>\(x \geq 5\)</item>
      <item>\(y \geq 2\)</item>
      <item>\(x \geq 2\)</item>
    </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x \geq 2\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which of the following represents the range of the function graphed below?
    
    <figure><media alt="GRAPH OF A LINE FOR ALL X GREATER THAN OR EQUAL TO 2, WITH POINT SHOWN AT (2 5), AND PASSING THROUGH THE POINTS (3, 8) AND (5, 14)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a79cc63c6acdd168fd53633b75e6c1594d031438"/></media></figure></item>
    </list>
    <list>
      <item>\(y \geq 5\)</item>
      <item>\(x \geq 5\)</item>
      <item>\(y \geq 2\)</item>
      <item>\(x \geq 2\)</item>
    </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(y \geq 5\) </para></section>
